 "https://www.e-n.org.uk/world-news/2019-09-indonesia-cannibals-come-to-christ-in-papua"}, {"title": "bisa dihargai rp30 juta mengapa babi jadi hewan yang disakralkan di papua", "url": "https://www.goodnewsfromindonesia.id/2021/08/16/bisa-dihargai-rp30-juta-mengapa-babi-jadi-hewan-yang-disakralkan-di-papua"}]}, "The search didn't turn up a direct source on how the Yali raise pigs, so the answer is partial.\n\n- **Where the Yali live:** Yali are a major tribal group in Highland Papua, Indonesia, and live to the east of the Baliem Valley in the Papuan highlands, mainly in Yalimo Regency, Yahukimo Regency, and the surrounding regencies.\n- **Pigs in Yali culture:** One reference is a 2023 journal article titled \"'Ap Lisurug' Mekanisme Pertukaran Babi dalam Budaya Yali\" (pig exchange mechanisms in Yali culture), published in *Cenderawasih: Jurnal Antropologi Papua*. Its title indicates pig exchange is part of Yali culture, but the search returned only the citation, not its content.\n- **Pigs in the wider region:** The search mostly returned material on other Papuan groups. A Papuan news piece says pigs are valuable domesticated animals for Papuan communities. It also notes that a single adult pig can be worth Rp30 million, but it refers to the Dani people of the Baliem Valley, not the Yali.\n\nFor specifics on Yali pig-keeping (housing, husbandry, role in exchange and ceremonies), the 2023 *Cenderawasih* article is the most promising lead, and I'd recommend reading it directly."], "durationSeconds": 5.720391458, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Xpo9PHH7rPCjad2n361ar4", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
